## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a secure, multi-account GitOps pipeline with image signing, SBOM attestations, and policy enforcement, plus real-world rollback.

## Key Concepts
- GitOps with FluxCD, Helm
- Container image signing (cosign) and SBOM attestations
- Open Policy Agent (Gatekeeper) for policy checks
- Canary deployments and automatic rollback
- Multi-account IAM and artifact attestation storage

## Code Example
```javascript
// FluxCD HelmRelease (simplified)
{
  apiVersion: "helm.toolkit.fluxcd.io/v2beta1",
  kind: "HelmRelease",
  metadata: { name: "my-service", namespace: "default" },
  spec: {
    chart: { spec: { chart: "my-service", version: "1.2.3" } },
    values: {
      image: { repository: "123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/my-service", tag: "1.2.3" }
    }
  }
}
```

```javascript
// Gatekeeper constraint (simplified)
{
  apiVersion: "constraints.gatekeeper.sh/v1beta1",
  kind: "K8sRequiredLabels",
  metadata: { name: "require-app-label" },
  spec: { match: { kinds: [{ apiGroups: [""], kinds: ["Deployment"] }] }, parameters: { requiredLabels: ["app","version"] } }
